## I. Geometric Distribution

```{r geometric_simulation}
# 1. Set the probability of success
p <- 0.2

# 2. Generate 1000 random variables (trials to first success)
set.seed(42) # For reproducibility
x <- rgeom(1000, prob = p) + 1

# 3. Calculate basic statistics
mean_x <- mean(x)
var_x  <- var(x)
sd_x   <- sd(x)

# 4. Print formatted results
cat("Number of trials required to achieve first success:\n")
cat("Mean:", sprintf("%.2f", mean_x), "\n")
cat("Variance:", sprintf("%.2f", var_x), "\n")
cat("Standard Deviation:", sprintf("%.2f", sd_x), "\n")
```

### 5. Histogram of Results

```{r}
hist(x,
     breaks = seq(0.5, max(x) + 0.5, by = 1),
     col = "pink",
     border = "black",
     main = "Histogram of Geometric Distribution (Trials to First Success)",
     xlab = "Number of Trials",
     ylab = "Frequency")
```

